    "name": "scATAC-seq FASTQ to Count Matrix",
    "readme": "# Single-Cell ATAC-seq FASTQ to Count Matrix\nFor more details on concepts and parameters, please refer to the Galaxy [tutorial](https://gxy.io/GTN:T00335).\n\n## Inputs\nThis workflow needs 3 files as input\n- FASTQ containing all cell barcode sequences, usually R2\n- FASTQ containing forward reads, usually R1\n- FASTQ containing reverse reads, usually R3\n\n## Processing\n- Incorporates the cell barcodes from the barcodes FASTQ into forward and reverse reads ids, and outputs only 2 FASTQ files further processing.\n- Maps the paired-end reads with **BWA-MEM**\n- Creates a ATAC fragments file using **Sinto fragments** tool and sorts it position\n- Calls peaks using **MACS2** and selects unique narrow peaks\n- Builds an anndata object using **EpiScanpy** tool suite.\n\n## Output\n- An **Anndata** (h5ad) file in  containing count matrix of cells x  features (peaks)",
